  "question": {
    "text": "<p>The value of current&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">i</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></math> flowing from <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi></math> to <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi></math> in the circuit diagram is :</p><p><img src=\"assets\\qt0238_905ed4484274.png\" style=\"width: 300px; height: 224px;\" />&nbsp;&nbsp;</p>"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>5</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>25</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>75</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi></math>",
      "is_correct": true
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "D"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p><img src=\"assets\\st0238_9d196a9b208e.png\" style=\"width: 301px; height: 242px;\" />&nbsp;</p><p>The Diagram shown in the question represents the balanced wheatstone bridge. It satisfy the condition of balanced wheat stone bridge.<br />Multiplication of dimensionally opposite resistance is same.<br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>&#8658;</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn></math><br />When the circuit is balanced wheat stone bridge then current through the branch&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>B</mi><mi>D</mi></math>&nbsp;is zero, so it can be removed.</p><p>Now, after removing&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>B</mi><mi>D</mi></math>&nbsp;wire voltage across&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi><mi>C</mi></math>&nbsp;is&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>8</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi></math>.</p><p>So, current will be,</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">i</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>8</mn><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>A</mi></math>&nbsp;</p>"
  }
}